Here is a simple Rust function that converts an array of bytes to a two-digit lowercase hexadecimal string.

```rust
use std::str::FromStr;
use serde_json::Value;

pub fn solve(input: Value) -> Value {
    let input: Vec<u8> = match input {
        Value::Array(vec) => vec.into_iter().map(|x| x.as_u8()).collect(),
        _ => panic!("Expected an array of bytes"),
    };

    let hex_str: String = input.iter().map(|byte| format!("{:02x}", byte)).collect();

    Value::String(hex_str)
}
```

This function first checks if the input is an array of bytes. If it is, it converts each byte to a two-digit hexadecimal string and concatenates them. If the input is not an array of bytes, it panics.

Please note that this function assumes that the input is a single array of bytes. If the input can be a different format, you would need to modify the function accordingly.
